<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="robots" content="noindex">
<title>Quillmoor Cycle Works - inbox-core demo</title>
<style>
  :root {
    color-scheme: light dark;
    --bg: #f5f3ee; --surface: #ffffff; --text: #1f2328; --muted: #57606a;
    --line: #dcd7cc; --brand: #23514a; --on-brand: #ffffff; --accent: #fff4d6; --accent-line: #e6c86e;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #15181c; --surface: #1d2227; --text: #e6e8eb; --muted: #a3acb6;
      --line: #313840; --brand: #2f6b62; --on-brand: #ffffff; --accent: #2e2a1c; --accent-line: #7a6631;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { margin: 0; font: 16px/1.55 system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif; color: var(--text); background: var(--bg); }
  .demo-banner { background: var(--accent); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--accent-line); padding: 10px 16px; text-align: center; font-size: 14px; }
  header { background: var(--brand); color: var(--on-brand); padding: 28px 16px; }
  header .inner, main { max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  header h1 { margin: 0; font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.2; }
  header p { margin: 6px 0 0; opacity: 0.9; }
  main { padding: 24px 16px 140px; }
  section { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 10px; padding: 16px 18px; margin: 0 0 16px; }
  h2 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 18px; }
  ul { margin: 8px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; }
  li { margin: 4px 0; }
  q { font-style: italic; }
  .muted { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="demo-banner" role="note"><strong>This is a demo.</strong> Quillmoor Cycle Works is a made-up shop, and its answers come from a made-up knowledge base. Conversations are deleted within a day; please do not type personal details.</div>
<header>
  <div class="inner">
    <h1>Quillmoor Cycle Works</h1>
    <p>Repairs, rentals and parts in the fictional town of Quillmoor.</p>
  </div>
</header>
<main>
  <section>
    <h2>Try the chat</h2>
    <p>Open the chat bubble in the corner. Some things to ask:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><q>What are your opening hours?</q> is answered from the shop's own information, with the entry it used.</li>
      <li><q>My gears keep skipping, what can I try?</q> is drafted, and a mechanic approves it before you see it.</li>
      <li><q>I want my money back</q>, a booking, or anything about safety goes straight to a person.</li>
      <li><q>Write me a poem about the sea</q> is not something the shop does, so it is passed on rather than made up.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>How it decides</h2>
    <p>A model reads each message and reports what it is about. Whether it may be answered is then decided by fixed rules, never by the model, so telling the assistant to ignore its instructions has nothing to change. When it is unsure, or anything fails, the message goes to a person.</p>
    <p class="muted">Built on inbox-core, an open-source inbox assistant core, with Chatwoot for the chat. Messages are rate limited, and the demo stops calling the model once its daily budget is spent.</p>
  </section>
</main>
<script>
  (function (d, t) {
    var BASE_URL = "{{CHATWOOT_ORIGIN}}";
    var g = d.createElement(t), s = d.getElementsByTagName(t)[0];
    g.src = BASE_URL + "/packs/js/sdk.js";
    g.async = true;
    s.parentNode.insertBefore(g, s);
    g.onload = function () {
      window.chatwootSDK.run({ websiteToken: "{{WEBSITE_TOKEN}}", baseUrl: BASE_URL });
    };
  })(document, "script");
</script>
</body>
</html>
